## Collapse Explorer Delta expansion into one RT statement

Context: Explorer's Delta/Lakehouse expansion submitted one query per BFS
level and then fetched triples in 250-entity batches. A fixed-depth CTE chain
now traverses and retrieves the bounded subgraph in one Query Warehouse
statement while other graph backends retain their existing traversal.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   Generate bounded forward/reverse BFS levels and fetch triples in one SQL statement.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   Dispatch to the Delta capability while preserving fallback and API metadata.
3. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_flat_store.py
   Cover SQL levels, traversal directions, bounds, escaping, and capping.
4. tests/units/dtwin/test_filter_expand.py
   Cover capability dispatch, fallback, relationship exclusion, errors, and columns.
5. docs/get-started.md and docs/features.md
   Document the bounded single-statement Delta/Lakehouse expansion path.
6. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-11-explorer-single-statement-expansion-design.md
   Record the approved architecture and safety constraints.
7. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-11-explorer-single-statement-expansion.md
   Record the test-driven implementation and verification sequence.

