## Port Spark SPARQL fail-closed fix from 0.8.1 (#167)

Context:
Task 5 ports the fully reviewed Spark SPARQL safety fix from `0.8.1`
(verified at commit `5b9beb82`) into the active `0.9.0` worktree without
altering existing unrelated in-progress changes. The port includes the
capability validator, translator hardening, translator/validator regression
tests, and additive architecture + user guide updates for the Spark support
boundary.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlCapabilityValidator.py
   Added the fail-closed SPARQL algebra validator (supported subset whitelist + unsupported feature rejection).
2. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlTranslator.py
   Integrated capability preflight validation and aligned specialized UNION gating with reviewed `0.8.1` behavior.
3. tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_capability_validator.py
   Added direct validator acceptance and rejection coverage, including alias and UNION-shape boundaries.
4. tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_translator_units.py
   Added fail-closed translator regressions, OPTIONAL semantics checks, alias coverage, and stricter success assertions.
5. docs/architecture.md
   Documented the Spark SPARQL fail-closed boundary (supported subset, rejected constructs, and fallback caveat).
6. docs/user-guide.md
   Added an Explorer-facing Spark SPARQL support boundary section (kept additive for Task 6 verification).

